{
	title: 'Effort snaps to the nearest level; /effort and completion',
	spec: `A requested effort the model lacks snaps to the nearest supported level instead of failing, everywhere a selection is resolved: /model, /effort, the picker, spawn's model argument, the config model setting and model switches. One function in src/host/effort.ts (replacing validate's throw) ranks the vocabulary none 0, minimal 1, low 2, medium 3, high 4, xhigh 5, max 6 and picks the supported level with the smallest rank distance; a tie rounds up, so thinking is never turned off unless none was asked for. Examples: max on GPT-5.5 gives xhigh; xhigh on Claude 4.6 gives max; minimal on GPT-6 Sol gives low; none on Opus 5.5 gives low. A model without effort control drops the effort. Every snap is reported, never silent: the spawn result and the /model reply say e.g. 'max → xhigh (closest supported)'. Words outside the vocabulary (typos) stay errors listing the model's levels, returned to a model as a tool error.

ultra is a hidden alias for max: accepted wherever a level is, absent from completion and /help, and reported as 'ultra → max (Hal has no Ultra mode; ask for subagents in the prompt)'. Codex's Ultra means max plus parallel subagents; Hal does not copy that.

Effort lives in the model string: config.ason's model holds provider/id or alias with an optional :level suffix, written only when the effort differs from the model's default. Selecting the default level clears the override; default and the default's level name are one choice, not two. Switching to an unqualified model carries a pinned effort over, snapped to the new model's levels; with no pin the new model's default applies.

/effort <level> changes only the current model's effort; /effort alone shows the current effort and the levels. It is listed in /help. Tab completion: /effort completes the current model's levels, default first as 'default (<level>)'; /model offers ':<level>' entries for the current model first, then model ids; after alias: or id: it completes that model's levels. /model :level equals /effort level.

Tests: nearest-level ranking including ties and none, ultra alias, snap reported by spawn, carry-over on model switch, typo still errors.`,
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['w7', 'pv'],
	foldInto: ['w7']
}
